<title>RUSSIA: Russian average wage rose 55 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Russian average wage rose 55 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian average monthly wages rose to 800,000 roubles ($143) in 1996, 55 percent above the average level in 1995, the State Statistics Committee said.</p>
<p>The committee said 22 percent of the population was living on less than the monthly subsistence income, which averaged 369,000 roubles in 1996.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520 ($ = 5613 Russian Roubles)</p>
</text>
